# library.api.key — centralized MCP provider API keys
#
# HOW TO USE
#   1. Copy this committed template to ./library.api.key in the project root:
#        cp library.api.key.example library.api.key
#   2. Fill in only the keys you need. Every worker command reads this file
#      automatically at startup (npm run providers, library:*, ...).
#   3. ./library.api.key is Git-ignored and must NEVER be committed, pasted
#      into chat/issues/logs, or shared. If a key was exposed anywhere,
#      revoke it and create a new one before use.
#
# PRECEDENCE AND SAFETY
#   - Variables already present in the process environment always win over
#     this file (CI secrets keep working unchanged).
#   - Only the provider variables listed below are read from this file;
#     anything else in it is ignored with a warning.
#   - Key values are never logged, never printed, and never persisted.
#     Run `npm run providers:keys` for a presence-only status table.
#
# APPLICATION SECRETS (DATABASE_URL, AUTH_SECRET, EMBEDDING_API_KEY) DO NOT
# BELONG HERE — they belong to the web app, not provider sync. Keep them in
# .env as documented in .env.example.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# MCP PROVIDER CATALOG KEYS
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Official MCP Registry (registry.modelcontextprotocol.io)
# No API key required. Used by: providers:sync, providers:check.

# Glama — REQUIRED since 2026-08-26 (the documented MCP API rejects
# unauthenticated requests). Create a key at:
#   https://glama.ai/settings/api-keys
# Used by: providers:sync-glama (Authorization: Bearer).
# Glama API data is governed by Glama's API Data License: visible attribution
# and links to each record's Glama listing are required when data is displayed.
GLAMA_API_KEY=

# Optional Glama API base override. Leave unset to use the documented default.
GLAMA_API_BASE_URL=https://glama.ai/api/mcp/v1

# MCPMarket — optional. The public sitemap importer needs no key; this token
# is only used by the read-only `providers:mcpmarket-auth-check` (GET /me).
# Create a token per: https://docs.mcpmarket.com/docs/api-tokens/using-api-tokens
MCPMARKET_API_KEY=

# Optional MCPMarket API base override.
MCPMARKET_API_BASE_URL=https://app.mcpmarket.com/api/v1

# GitHub enrichment — optional. Raises the public GitHub API quota for
# metadata enrichment. Use a NEW, minimum-scope fine-grained token kept only
# here or in a secret manager. Create one at:
#   https://github.com/settings/personal-access-tokens/new
# Used by: providers:sync --enrich-github, library:enrich.
GITHUB_TOKEN=

# Awesome MCP Servers — no API key required (fixture/markdown import).
